<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Faiz Talab Khan</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1829</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Faiz Talab Khan was a Pathan of the Barech tribe who served the British <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-india-company">East India Company</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-anglo-maratha-war">Second Anglo-Maratha War</a>. In 1804 the British rewarded him with the district of Pataudi, near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/delhi">Delhi</a>, making him the first Nawab of Pataudi State. His descendants ruled until 1947, among them the cricket-captain Nawabs <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iftikhar-ali-khan-pataudi">Iftikhar Ali Khan Pataudi</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mansoor-ali-khan-pataudi">Mansoor Ali Khan Pataudi</a>.</p></div>
